\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. THE sands of time are sinking;
\par The dawn of heaven breaks;
\par The summer morn I've sighed for,
\par The fair, sweet morn, awakes,
\par Dark, dark hath been the midnight;
\par But day-spring is at hand, 
\par And glory, glory dwelleth
\par In Immanuel's land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The King there, in His beauty,
\par Without a veil is seen;
\par It were a well-spent journey,
\par Though seven deaths lay between:
\par The Lamb, with His fair army,
\par Doth on Mount Zion stand,
\par And glory, glory dwelleth
\par In Immanuel's land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Christ! He is the fountain,
\par The deep, sweet well of love;
\par The streams on earth I've tasted
\par More deep I'll drink above;
\par There to an ocean fullness
\par His mercy doth expand,
\par And glory, glory dwelleth
\par In Immanuel's land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With mercy and with judgement
\par My web of time He wove,
\par And aye the dews of sorrow
\par Were lustred by His love;
\par I'll bless the hand that guided,
\par I'll bless the hand that planned,
\par When throned where glory dwelleth
\par In Immanuel's land.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

